{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XHSfxtsyEpftD3uymfZAb4","type":"tool_result","content":"30\t\n31\t-- Imports from Agda and the Agda Standard Library -----------------------------\n32\topen import Agda.Primitive               using () renaming ( Set to Type )\n33\topen import Level                        using ( Level ; _⊔_ )\n34\t\n35\t-- Imports from the Agda Universal Algebra Library -----------------------------\n36\topen import Overture.Signatures          using ( 𝓥 )\n37\t\n38\tprivate variable a b ρ : Level\n39\t```\n40\t-->\n41\t\n42\t```agda\n43\t-- The type of I-ary operations on A.  Arity first, carrier second, so that\n44\t-- `Op (Fin 2)` partially applies as \"the type of binary operations\" on any given A.\n45\tOp : Type 𝓥 → Type a → Type (a ⊔ 𝓥)\n46\tOp I A = (I → A) → A\n47\t```\n48\t\n49\tFor example, the `I`-*ary projection operations* on `A` are represented as\n50\tinhabitants of the type `Op I A` as follows.\n51\t\n52\t```agda\n53\t-- Example (projections)\n54\tπ : {I : Type 𝓥} {A : Type a } → I → Op I A\n55\tπ i = λ x → x i\n56\t```\n57\t\n58\tOccasionally we want to extract the arity of a given operation symbol.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b18e304-1c10-49e4-bf2e-315ae502d56d","uuid":"ec4a6527-2d3e-4929-b51b-3de8d3e840a6","timestamp":"2026-09-25T05:56:35.858Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/nix/store/0mkdwhwzshgsa7xknd81r8hvdp6gbmr6-agda-algebras-unstable-2026-09-07/src/Overture/Operations.lagda.md","content":"\n-- Imports from Agda and the Agda Standard Library -----------------------------\nopen import Agda.Primitive               using () renaming ( Set to Type )\nopen import Level                        using ( Level ; _⊔_ )\n\n-- Imports from the Agda Universal Algebra Library -----------------------------\nopen import Overture.Signatures          using ( 𝓥 )\n\nprivate variable a b ρ : Level\n```\n-->\n\n```agda\n-- The type of I-ary operations on A.  Arity first, carrier second, so that\n-- `Op (Fin 2)` partially applies as \"the type of binary operations\" on any given A.\nOp : Type 𝓥 → Type a → Type (a ⊔ 𝓥)\nOp I A = (I → A) → A\n```\n\nFor example, the `I`-*ary projection operations* on `A` are represented as\ninhabitants of the type `Op I A` as follows.\n\n```agda\n-- Example (projections)\nπ : {I : Type 𝓥} {A : Type a } → I → Op I A\nπ i = λ x → x i\n```\n\nOccasionally we want to extract the arity of a given operation symbol.\n","numLines":30,"startLine":30,"totalLines":65}}}
